<!-- GH-1034, P3 call guards, option persistcalls. churn reads, then
     writes, each of 256 writable globals, with a call after every write and
     one more inside a branch every eighth step: 288 calls. small touches two
     globals across three calls. Pass 1 is upstream placement (option off):
     every global is guarded at every call, and the guards survive dead-code
     removal, so churn's live IR holds 84250 ops. Pass 2 is the default:
     churn's pass guards 319 RAM ranges at 288 calls (91,872 guards), past the
     65,536-guard threshold, so each global keeps only the guards at the call
     before its read and the call after its write, 542 of its 73,728, and the
     live IR drops to 3159 ops; the skipped guards and joins keep their op
     numbers, so every pass creates 95006. small, far below the threshold,
     keeps every guard. Pass 3 is persistcalls on: small loses one guard that
     only hands a value to the next (16 ops to 15). Each function prints the
     same body in every pass. Two
     more passes count churn's ops only: at persistcalls 91873, one guard more
     than churn's pass, it keeps them; at 91872 it drops them. The fixture's
     source, provenance and native oracle are beside it.
-->
</binaryimage>
